      "writtenOn": "2024-12-18T07:02:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Discussed with markchien@. It seems this would be feasible, but one major concern is that the RTM_NEWADDR event is asynchronous. If two downstream addresses are allocated back-to-back, this might increase the chance of conflict since we will need to wait for the RTM_NEWADDR event to detect the conflict. However, for now, downstream addresses are added to the database only when requested, so this issue should not occur.\nReopen if any idea.",
      "parentUuid": "82791653_5f15e7ec",
      "revId": "981bf1a297f84ba40ba5f775de24cdbee739fbdc",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
